        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0562" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/10833.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Solicitor Folk.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 31, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">To the Solicitor</hi>: Replying to your inquiry as
                    to when Victoriano Huerta became Dictator of Mexico; I have consulted with
                    President Wilson, and find that he regards October 10th, 1913, as the date upon
                    which Victoriano Huerta became Dictator of Mexico, that being the date on which
                    he suspended the Constitution; assumed the power and authority delegated to
                    other officials; dissolved Congress, and caused a large number of the members of
                    the Mexican Congress to be imprisoned. From and after that date Victoriano
                    Huerta has been Dictator in the sense of the announcement of the President of
                    the United States that he will not recognize as legal or binding anything done
                    by Huerta since he became Dictator.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
